          <div class="faq-answer">
            <div class="faq-answer-content">
              Minimally invasive neurosurgery uses smaller incisions, specialized instruments, and real-time imaging or endoscopic visualization to treat brain and spine conditions with less disruption to surrounding tissue. Compared to traditional open surgery, patients typically experience less pain, shorter hospital stays, and faster return to daily activities.
